 "method": {
  "line": "MEMBRANE'S OWN LINE, AND DEBT SIZED TO IT (owner rulings 2026-10-18; lib/wavefront/membraneLine.ts): the per-wallet simulator's rule — weightedMembraneLine of the t0 collateral (MEMBRANE_ASSET_LTV, modelled: WETH 0.80, wstETH 0.78, WBTC 0.75, …; DEPLOY_LAUNCH_LTV, the deploy script's own: sUSDS 0.88, syrupUSDC 0.86, scrvUSD 0.86), value-weighted at t0, each asset clamped to its class cap. A position holding ANY collateral without a Membrane line is excluded ('no-membrane-line' / 'partial-membrane-line'). Each half's t0 debt is scaled by memLine / protocolLine (membraneDebtScale; protocolLine = the protocol's own line for the same legs: the whole position's when unsplit, else the LT-weighted line of the half's own legs); collateral unchanged. Lower for most positions, higher where Membrane's line is above the protocol's (mostly stablecoin collateral). An UNSPLIT position sits the same proportional distance past Membrane's line as it sat past the protocol's, so its t0 decision is the protocol's own; a SPLIT position keeps that only per half, so a half can open under its own line. The protocol's line (Aave weighted LT, Morpho LLTV) stays in each row as `line`: it locates t0 and is the sensitivity 'Membrane at the protocol's line'.",
  "liquidity": "LIQUIDITY-CAPPED SALES (owner ruling 2026-10-18; lib/wavefront/liquidity.ts, meta.liquidity): every sale is an order offered to a shared per-(chain, token) book that allows 0.98x († modelled: 0.98×, the unweighted mean of the three measured class medians of depth recovery 8h after five crashes (membrane-datasets q28/liquidity-recovery REPORT.md; the report itself rates those medians too generous and recommends lower values — see the sensitivity rows)) the most tokens liquidators absorbed in any rolling 10 minutes of the window, at any minute, in order minute then pid. The order splits across collateral legs pro rata by value; each leg fills against its own book. The unfilled part stays pending: while it is, the timer is idle, the order is re-sized each minute at that minute’s price (never more than pending, never past the borrow cap: back at or under the cap cancels it) and the LTV moves on the collateral still held. A remainder still pending at the grid end is never credited. A position that would have to sell a token with no observed liquidity on its chain is excluded (no-capacity).",
  "comparison": "THE SHARE OF DEBT CLOSED (owner rulings 2026-10-18): the two sides carry different debt, so dollars do not compare; each side is its repaid debt over its own t0 debt, debt-weighted over the priced compared positions (census.ts censusShares; meta.totals.*.shares). Debt repaid only: Membrane’s liquidation fee cannot be assumed, so no collateral-seized figure is compared; real seized stays in each row as provenance. Real repaid dollars are the size of the day, never set beside Membrane dollars."
 },
